Test fixtures
=============

annotation/
-----------
Small pieces of real genome annotations and the matching sequence records, cut without any change of the
lines that were kept. They are used by test-annotation.R to test retrieve_longest_isoforms(), select_orthologs()
and generate_ortholog_tables() on the file layouts of NCBI RefSeq and Ensembl.

ncbi_ecoli_sakai.gff, ncbi_ecoli_sakai_protein.faa
    NCBI RefSeq GFF3 and protein FASTA of Escherichia coli O157:H7 str. Sakai, assembly GCF_000008865.2 (ASM886v2):
    the header lines, the 'region' line of the chromosome and all features of the loci ECs_0001 - ECs_0040,
    ECs_0083, ECs_0084, ECs_0621 and ECs_0684 (44 loci, 39 of them with a protein). The piece holds loci without a
    gene symbol and three pairs of loci that share a symbol (dnaJ: ECs_0015 / ECs_0684, mokC: ECs_0016 / ECs_0621,
    fruR: ECs_0083 / ECs_0084).
ncbi_ecoli_k12.gtf, ncbi_ecoli_k12_protein.faa
    NCBI RefSeq GTF and protein FASTA of Escherichia coli str. K-12 substr. MG1655, assembly GCF_000005845.2
    (ASM584v2): the header lines and all features of the genes b0001 - b0035 (34 with a protein).
    Source of both: https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/genomes/all/GCF/ (NCBI RefSeq).
    Licence: NCBI places no restrictions on the use or distribution of its molecular data (public domain,
    https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/home/about/policies/).

ensembl_human_chr21.gtf, ensembl_human_chr21.gff3, ensembl_human_chr21_pep.fa, ensembl_human_chr21_cds.fa
    Ensembl release 115, Homo sapiens GRCh38, chromosome 21: the header lines and all features of nine genes -
    five protein-coding genes with three coding transcripts each (ENSG00000160233, ENSG00000160180,
    ENSG00000166265, ENSG00000160202, ENSG00000157542), two protein-coding genes with one (ENSG00000286224,
    ENSG00000186980), one immunoglobulin gene (ENSG00000277282, gene_biotype IG_V_gene) and one lncRNA gene
    (ENSG00000184385) - with their records of the 'pep.all' (18 proteins) and 'cds.all' (17 coding sequences)
    FASTA files. The IDs of the FASTA headers carry versions (ENSP00000284885.3, ENST00000284885.8); the GTF
    gives versions in fields of their own, the GFF3 in the attribute 'version'.
    Source: https://ftp.ensembl.org/pub/release-115/ (gtf/homo_sapiens, gff3/homo_sapiens, fasta/homo_sapiens).
    Licence: Ensembl imposes no restrictions on access to, or use of, its data
    (https://www.ensembl.org/info/about/legal/disclaimer.html).

The pieces were cut from the copies of these files that the second audit of the package downloaded
(/home/claude/audit2/work/r05 and /home/claude/audit2/work/iso on the machine of the audit).

codon_aln/
----------
pair1_pal2nal.aln, pair2_pal2nal.aln, pair3_pal2nal.aln, pair7_pal2nal.aln
    The PAL2NAL codon alignments (FASTA) of the 1st, 2nd, 3rd and 7th gene pair of the example data of the package
    (inst/seqs/ortho_thal_cds.fasta vs inst/seqs/ortho_lyra_cds.fasta), as dNdS() builds them with the protein
    alignments of orthologr <= 0.4.3 (Needleman-Wunsch without substitution matrix).
golden_values.tsv
    dN, dS and dN/dS of these alignments: Comeron (gestimator; it writes four significant digits) and Li
    (seqinr::kaks) as computed by orthologr 0.5.0, and MLPB as computed by KaKs_Calculator 2.0 (bioconda build)
    for the cross-check. Comeron and Li agree with MLPB within 12% for dN and dS on these pairs; the test states
    a tolerance of 15% (or 0.005).
known_pairs.tsv
    The 20 reciprocal best hit pairs of the example data with their Comeron dN, dS and dN/dS (same alignments).
    Written by /home/claude/tools-h/scripts/mk_golden.R on the machine of the second audit round.

hits/
-----
tie_break_hits.tsv, tie_break_expected.tsv
    A hand-written hit table in the 21-column format of diamond() / blast() in which every level of the best-hit
    rules decides once, and the best hit expected under best_hit_rule = "bitscore" and "evalue".

dnds_0.4.3/
-----------
comeron_20.rds, yn_20.rds
    The tables dNdS() of orthologr 0.4.3 (drostlab/orthologr, commit 06c3098) returns for the 20-gene example of
    the package (inst/seqs/ortho_thal_cds.fasta against ortho_lyra_cds.fasta) with its defaults and
    dnds_est.method = "Comeron" / "YN", as plain data.frames, with the versions that made them. Made on
    2026-11-13 by make_fixture.R (same folder) with DIAMOND 2.2.8, KaKs_Calculator 2.0 and R 4.5.3.
    test-legacy.R compares them with what this version returns with the options that restore the defaults of
    0.4.3 (see NEWS.md).
